spoint wireweave HOST must mirror the joiner's existing-open-peer catch-up loop, or a joined peer appears on the host (nostr presence) but cannot play. client/app.js host bridge (the _wwRoom && !_wwJoin branch) attaches bridge.data.addEventListener('peer-open', ...) to call client.attachWireweavePeer(pk,dc) -> BrowserServer posts PEER_CONNECT -> WorkerEntry.js PEER_CONNECT handler news a PeerTransport + _ctx.onClientConnect(t) -> ServerHandlers.onClientConnect spawns the player and sends HANDSHAKE_ACK/snapshots. THE BUG (fixed 34101551): the host had ONLY the peer-open listener, NO catch-up sweep over already-open peers and NO retry if dc was null at announce. WireweaveJoinClient.connect() and WireweaveTransport BOTH guard the mirror direction by iterating bridge.data.peers for peer?.dc?.readyState==='open'. So if the joiner datachannel opened before the host wired its listener (race), or peer-open fired with dc still establishing, the host never called attachWireweavePeer and the joiner was never spawned -> uncontrollable. FIX: idempotent _attachIfReady(pk) {if attached return; dc=peers.get(pk)?.dc; if(!dc||dc.readyState!=='open')return; attached.add; client.attachWireweavePeer(pk,dc)} + a catch-up loop `for ([pk,peer] of bridge.data.peers) if (peer?.dc?.readyState==='open') _attachIfReady(pk)` + a retry on the 'data' event + _attached.delete on peer-close. window.__app.wwPeers() exposes {peers,attached} for witness. RULE: any new datachannel-attach listener on the wireweave bridge needs the existing-open-peer catch-up + dc-ready guard, because peer-open ordering vs dc-open is not guaranteed. Also fixed same commit: landing share link doubled /spoint//spoint/demo.html when content.json demo_href was absolute (concat of pathname+demoBase); fix = new URL(demoBase, location.href).